plan.angle:
VARIATION-FIRST WITH VISIBLE-REALISM GRAFTS: one shared pure coat library plus a composer recipe v2 species/individual split, which together give within-species variety in both the composer and planetary fauna. On top of that, the audit's most visible composer realism defects get local fixes:
- head/neck helmet step;
- limb-root collar blobs;
- kinked joints;
- round stick legs with no muscle mass;
- wrong quadruped footfall;
- foot stomp and pitch pop;
- swinging theropod arms;
- inverted giraffe pattern;
- mirror-symmetric coats;
- scaled-adult juveniles.

plan.thesis:
What the dossier measured:
- Same-recipe composer animals are vertex-identical: colorSeed geometry delta 0; rhino colorSeed 400 vs 7777 AE 0.
- Coats are exactly mirror-symmetric: L/R dRGB 0 over 558-737 pairs.
- A planet shows at most 4 coat schemes.
- Planet individuals differ by only 3-4% RMSE, and juveniles are scaled adults.
- Perceived variety is driven first by coat colour and pattern, then by silhouette proportion (size, sex, age), then by motion desync.

The increment therefore builds two foundations first:
1. a pure, three-free coat library (pattern families, region marks, 8 natural pigment families, seeded per-individual drift, true 3D lateral sampling) that the composer AND the planet (through the digest-safe shared presentation files) both consume;
2. composer recipe v2 with an individual channel (individualSeed, sex, maturity, condition), correlated bounded deltas, allometry and a coherent random-species generator.

Realism is grafted where it is local, cheap and measurable:
- composer skin: neck-to-head blend rings, 4-ring limb roots with graded weights, splined centrelines, dorsal/lateral muscle lobes and condyles, higher limb and torso tessellation;
- composer rig: lateral-sequence footfall, zero-velocity Hermite swing with soft touchdown, continuous foot pitch, cos-phased arm swing gated by arm type, consistent many-legged knee pole, allometric limb robustness, size-scaled breathing;
- planet: neonatal juveniles with continuous maturity, sex dimorphism, family-envelope clamps.

Every realism change is also parameterised per individual, so the two goals land as the same code.

Expected measurable gains:
- same-preset herd pairwise RMSE 0.1% -> at least 4%;
- planet variant RMSE 3-4% -> at least 6%;
- coat schemes per planet 4 -> at least 8;
- coherent random constraint rate 89% -> at most 25%;
- collar weight step 1.0 -> at most 0.4;
- neck/head radius jump 1.58 -> at most 1.15;
- foot pitch step 16-25 deg -> at most 4 deg;
- touchdown vertical speed down at least 4x.

