STEP 1: src/fauna-coat-fields.ts.
- Use an integer lattice hash (pcg3d-style with Math.imul and >>>0), NOT string hashing; legacy noise3 does 27 string hashes per call.
- Export: hash3u(x,y,z,seed): uint32; valueNoise3; fbm2; worley3(x,y,z,seed,out) writing F1, F2 and the nearest cell hash into a caller-provided array (no allocation).
- CoatGenome = {version:'fauna-coat-1', pattern (resolved, never 'auto'), marks:int 0-255, scale 0.5-2, contrast 0-1.5, countershade 0-1, bellyLine (dorsal threshold, default -0.45), colours: Record<role, [r,g,b] linear>, markRole: 'accent'|'belly' (dark or light marks), seed:uint32, warp 0-1, threshold offset, juvenileSpots 0-1, greying 0-1}.
- CoatSample = {x, y, z (metres / bodyLength, bind space, z SIGNED), dorsal -1..1, region: CoatRegion, along 0..1 within the region}.

Colour helpers:
- coatSpeciesColours(paletteId, colorSeed): linear RGB per role, from stream composerHash-compatible string `coat-species-v1/${paletteId}/${colorSeed}`. Apply hue ±0.04, saturation ×(1±0.12), value ×(1±0.10) in HSV, so a grey keeps saturation near 0.
- Clamp linear luminance per role: base/accent/belly/skin within 0.02-0.60, keratin ≤ 0.5.
- Implement the sRGB↔linear and HSV conversions locally (no three).

coatIndividualDrift(key, variability):
- stream `coat-individual-v1/${key}`;
- hue ±0.015v, value ±8%v, saturation ±10%v;
- new seed; scale ×(1±0.08v); threshold ±0.06v; warp jitter;
- greying 0-0.3v;
- rare morphs: melanistic p=0.012v (value ×0.35), leucistic 0.004v (saturation ×0.25, value → 0.55 lum cap), erythristic 0.008v (hue +0.04, saturation ×1.2);
- v = 0 returns the identity drift (all deltas 0, same seed).
applyCoatDrift(genome, drift) returns a new genome.

evaluateCoat(genome, sample, out: number[] | Float32Array, offset = 0): void. Writes linear RGB, allocates nothing in the hot path, and reuses module-level scratch.
- The pattern mask m (0..1) is evaluated in 3D at q = (x,y,z) × cellsPerBody × scale, with cellsPerBody per pattern: spots 11, rosettes 8, reticulated 6.5, stripes 4.5 (period), bands 3, saddle n/a, dorsal-stripe n/a, dapple 12, piebald 2.2, roan 60, brindle 9.
- Patterns:
  - spots: 1 - smooth(r0, r0+soft, F1) with r0 = 0.28 ± 0.06 per cell (cell hash);
  - rosettes: ring band 0.55 < F1/r < 0.9 broken by valueNoise gaps, centre tinted at 0.35;
  - reticulated: m = smooth(0.05, 0.10, F2-F1), so the PATCHES take the mark colour and the thin lines take the belly/light role (dark patches separated by pale lines, fixing the inverted legacy savanna);
  - stripes: sin(2π(u + warp·fbm)) thresholded, with width varying 0.6-1.4 per band, where u = x on torso/neck/tail and along on limbs (rings on legs), fading toward the belly;
  - bands: transverse rings with per-band width jitter;
  - saddle: a dorsal blanket on x within [-0.25, 0.25] of the body and dorsal > 0.1;
  - dorsal-stripe: |z| < 0.04 and dorsal > 0.6;
  - dapple: light F1 inverse;
  - piebald: thresholded fbm using the belly role (white patches);
  - roan: high-frequency white flecks;
  - brindle: thin warped dark streaks.
- Region marks are added by bit:
  - socks: limb-lower and foot darken toward accent, or lighten when markRole is belly;
  - mask: head and muzzle;
  - blaze: a frontal |z| < 0.05 stripe on head/muzzle using belly;
  - tail-tip: the tail-tip region;
  - tail-rings: bands on tail;
  - ear-tips: ear with along > 0.7;
  - rump-patch: torso x < -0.35 and dorsal > -0.2, using belly;
  - juvenile-spots: 2 dorsolateral rows of small light spots on the torso, strength genome.juvenileSpots.
- Countershading: mix toward belly by countershade × smooth(bellyLine+0.3, bellyLine-0.3, dorsal); limbs get 0.5× countershading.
- Greying lightens the muzzle.
- Grain ±4% from valueNoise at 40 cells per body.
- No mark is applied on horn, eye or armor regions (armor uses the plate role).

Other exports:
- coatMeanColor(genome): an area-weighted mean over a fixed canonical 512-point sample of a unit capsule body plus 4 limbs, used for the far LOD.
- coatMinFeature(genome): the smallest mark feature in body-length units, so consumers can clamp scale to vertex spacing.
- defaultCoatGenome(paletteId, colorSeed, overrides) maps legacy palettes, with AUTO_PATTERN resolving 'auto'.
- FAUNA_COAT_FIELD_VERSION = 'fauna-coat-1'.

STEP 2: tests/fauna-coat-swatches.mjs renders unwrapped swatches: 13 patterns × 3 individuals, plus an 8-mark row and a legacy reference row that re-implements mesh.ts:164-178 inline. Size 256×128 each, written with node:zlib to test-results/wp1-swatches-<n>/coat-swatches.png and report.json with the timings. Never reuse an existing output directory.

acceptance:
Coverage at scale 1:
- spots dark fraction 0.12-0.35;
- reticulated dark-patch fraction ≥ 0.6 and pale-line fraction 0.12-0.30;
- rosettes ring darkness exceeds centre darkness by ≥ 0.1;
- stripes dark fraction 0.25-0.5.

