STEP 4, src/fauna-composer-individual.ts (pure, three-free).

composerIndividualTraits(recipe) → ComposerIndividualTraits. It reads ONLY the individual keys, species enums, variability, dimorphism, allometry and bodyLength rounded to 1e-3 (needed for allometry). This keeps it stable: traits computed from the species recipe and from the derived effective recipe must be equal (test this).
- Stream: composerRandom(`composer-individual-v2/${composerHash(encoded species keys except bodyLength)}/${individualSeed}`).
- Latents: z = clamp((u1+u2+u3-1.5)/0.5, -2, 2) for size, limb, neck, head, tail, mass and carriage.
- individualSeed 0 → every z = 0 and sex resolves to 'none' (type specimen).
- sex: 'auto' resolves by hash to female/male when dimorphism > 0 and seed > 0, else 'none'; explicit female/male is always honoured.
- Fields:
  - sex, maturity, condition;
  - size, limb, neck, head, tail, mass;
  - hornScale, hornCurl (±0.15v·z), hornAsym (0.02-0.05 × v, signed);
  - earScale (1 ± 0.15v), eyeScale (1 ± 0.08v, × (1+0.25(1-m)) for juveniles);
  - limbRadius (1 ± 0.10v + 0.04·condition);
  - segmentJitter [3] (±0.05v, for fore and hind separately);
  - torso {chest, belly, rump, waist, withers}, each a z × v value in [-2, 2];
  - carriage {neck ±0.12v rad, headPitch ±0.08v, tail ±0.15v};
  - motion {phase 0..1 (0 when seed 0), periodScale 1 ± 0.06v, dutyDelta ±0.03v, liftScale 1 ± 0.10v, breathPhase, lookPhase};
  - coat {driftKey: `${speciesHash}/${individualSeed}`, juvenileSpots};
  - countScale: osteoderm row offset -2..+2, plate count offset -2..+2, feather offset -1..+3;
  - allometry {limbRobust: (bodyLength/1)^(0.09·allometry), headRel: (bodyLength/1)^(-0.12·allometry), eyeRel: (bodyLength/1)^(-0.25·allometry)};
  - neutral: true iff seed 0, maturity 1, condition 0, sex none, allometry 0.

deriveComposerIndividual(recipe) → {recipe: effective, traits, deltas: string[]}. Numeric deltas use v = variability, are clamped to COMPOSER_RANGES, and every clamp is reported in deltas:
- bodyLength ×(1 + 0.04v·zSize);
- legLength ×(1 + 0.035v·zLimb - 0.01v·zMass);
- neckLength ×(1 + 0.05v·zNeck);
- headSize ×(1 + 0.04v·zHead) × headRel;
- snoutLength ×(1 + 0.05v·zHead);
- tailLength ×(1 + 0.06v·zTail), skipped when tail is none;
- girth ×(1 + 0.06·condition + 0.03v·zMass).
Sex, with d = dimorphism:
- male: bodyLength ×(1+0.10d), girth ×(1+0.05d), hornScale ×(1+0.35d);
- female: hornScale ×(1-0.6d).
Maturity m:
- bodyLength ×(0.45+0.55m), headSize ×(1+0.35(1-m)), snoutLength ×(0.7+0.3m);
- legLength ×(1+0.15(1-m)) for unguligrade and digitigrade legs;
- neckLength ×(0.75+0.25m), tailLength ×(0.8+0.2m);
- hornScale ×m², earScale ×(1+0.2(1-m));
- juvenileSpots = clamp((0.75-m)/0.4, 0, 1) when the marks bit 128 is set, else 0.
The neutral case returns effective deep-equal to the input and deltas = [].

